' From the text of Grogono's article (BYTE, July 1979, p. 203). Asks for
' numbers and prints their factorials until given zero or less.
' Transcribed from the scan: the only changes are ^ for the printed up
' arrow, straight quotes, spacing and line breaks outside strings, and these
' comment lines. Strings are as printed (spaces inside strings are read
' from proportional type, so their exact count is approximate).
' The article's sample dialogue shows the number typed after the prompt;
' the input is not echoed, so here the prompt and the answer share a line.
( "ENTER A NUMBER" M ? = M. ^
  N M. = 1 ( N. ^ N. * N N. 1 - = )
  "FACTORIAL (" M. ! ") = " ! "!" )
$$
